# runtime data
data/
.env

# eval corpus uploads — real document content, never commit
corpus/

# Eval reports ARE tracked - they are the evidence behind every number in
# eval/docs/, and a collaborator cannot check a tuning conclusion without
# them. Everything committed so far is HybridQA, a public dataset.
#
# BEFORE COMMITTING A REPORT FROM A PRIVATE CORPUS: reports embed the full
# chunk text of whatever was evaluated, so a run against real uploaded
# documents puts that content in git history permanently. Add an explicit
# ignore for it here first.
#
# The .jsonl sink is excluded because it duplicates the .json's `cases`
# array exactly (verified: same 125 cases, same keys). It exists so a run
# killed mid-sweep still leaves its cases on disk; the .json is written at
# the end and carries the same data plus the summary metrics.
eval/reports/*.jsonl
